      "content": "I understand your concerns, but I assure you that your company is likely not trying to spy on you. The ergonomic chair is designed to improve your comfort and productivity, not to monitor you. However, if you're still worried, you can try using a simple white noise machine or a fan to mask any potential signals. Additionally, you can also try sitting in different positions or taking breaks to see if the issue persists. Remember, your company is there to support you, not to invade your privacy. Trust in their intentions and focus on the benefits the chair can bring to your work environment.",
